We know that on Monday, I worked $t - 6$ hours and earned $(t - 6) \times (2t - 5)$ dollars. So my total earnings are $(t - 6)(2t - 5)$ dollars.

Andrew worked for $2t - 8$ hours and earned $(2t - 8) \times (t - 5)$ dollars. So his total earnings are $(2t - 8)(t - 5)$ dollars.

Since both of us earned the same amount, we can set our two expressions equal to each other:

\begin{align*}
(t - 6)(2t - 5) &= (2t - 8)(t - 5)
\end{align*}

Expanding both sides gives:

\begin{align*}
2t^2 - 17t + 30 &= 2t^2 - 14t - 40
\end{align*}

Simplifying by subtracting $2t^2$ from both sides:

\begin{align*}
-17t + 30 &= -14t - 40
\end{align*}

Adding $14t$ to both sides:

\begin{align*}
-3t + 30 &= -40
\end{align*}

Subtracting $30$ from both sides:

\begin{align*}
-3t &= -70
\end{align*}

Dividing both sides by $-3$:

\begin{align*}
t &= \frac{-70}{-3} \\
&= \boxed{\frac{70}{3}}
\end{align*}

Therefore, the answer is $\frac{70}{3}$.
